OL,3,GNEWSAPiles of fly-tipped waste cleared
OL,4,Afrom estate
OL,5,
OL,6,FWaste illegally dumped in the middle of
OL,7,Fa housing estate was at risk of
OL,8,Fexploding if set alight, a council has
OL,9,Fwarned.
OL,11,FTwo large piles of waste which included
OL,12,Fgas canisters, paint and medical
OL,13,Fequipment were fly-tipped on a playing
OL,14,Ffield in Dorset Avenue in Birtley,
OL,15,FGateshead, over the space of a week,
OL,16,Faccording to Gateshead Council.
OL,18,FIt began clearing the waste on
OL,19,FWednesday and said the 20 staff and 12
OL,20,Fvehicles, including tractors, needed to
OL,21,Fdo so would cost more than #20,000.
OL,23,APub: 14-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,397,390,260,160,0,100
